  "sources": {
    "archive": {
      "title": "Curated CMF_1960_1 archive snapshot",
      "locator": "ARCHIVE/artifacts/output/smoke_test/*_18-04-2026.json",
      "note": "Workbook-derived transcription associated with Så byggdes husen. Book edition, page, layer alternatives and exact period not independently verified. This compact copy is self-contained; no runtime archive access."
    },
    "era_context": {
      "title": "Boverket, typical 1960s three-storey lamellhus",
      "url": "https://www.boverket.se/sv/energiguiden/energieffektivisera-flerbostadshus/energirenovera/byggide/klarlagg-forutsattningarna/atgarder-i-typiska-byggnader/",
      "note": "General era context, not evidence for this exact typology. Describes 50–100 mm mineral wool in infill walls and ventilated facades, including board at balconies; uses 100 mm attic insulation in its pre-measure example."
    },
    "floor_finish": {
      "title": "Forbo Marmoleum technical dimensions",
      "url": "https://www.forbo.com/flooring/en-uk/commercial-products/marmoleum/marmoleum-solid/marmoleum-piano/bpvg7w?dnr=3607",
      "note": "Modern product plausibility comparison for assumed 2.5 mm linoleum, not proof of 1960s original material."
    },
    "thermal_conventions": {
      "title": "BRE BR443 (2019), U-value conventions",
      "url": "https://www.cibse.org/media/wzrjrf3l/conventions-for-u-value-calculations.pdf",
      "note": "Additional diagnostic cases use direction-specific surface resistance and ventilated facade exclusions. The retained schema's default films and area-weighted layer calculation are not a full ISO 6946/13370 assessment."
    }
  },
  "review_notes": [
    "Archive construction_year 1960 is name-derived. Reconstructed year 1965 is an assumed representative year within the provisional 1960s / SE.02 classification, not verified dating.",
    "Material conductivity, density and heat capacity are copied unchanged for reproducibility. High precision does not imply measured accuracy. Mineral-wool density 265 kg/m3 and EPS conductivity about 0.030 W/(mK) need verification before transient simulation.",
    "Legacy carbon records are preserved only because OpaqueMaterial requires them. Mappings and values are unreviewed and must not be used for carbon assessment. No carbon mapping services or source dependencies are introduced.",
    "All physical order corrections are reconstruction assumptions, not recovered book drawing sequences. Floors are ordered upper to lower for internal floor, ground to room for ground/slab, and attic to room for TOP_FLOOR.",
    "Separate facade variants replace simultaneous brick/board and duplicated gypsum entries. Assume a 25 mm facade cavity geometrically, not encoded as a fictitious solid material. Series-only baseline omits its resistance; dedicated diagnostic scenarios model unventilated and well-ventilated cavity treatments separately.",
    "TOP_FLOOR, not uninsulated ROOF covering, corresponds to the LoD1 effective Roof property. Archive ROOF covering is retained as an unreviewed physical stack with suspect 3 mm sheet and solid-batten assumptions, not a whole-roof heat-loss result.",
    "230 mm attic mineral wool and 85/60 mm EPS are preserved as observed archive data, not asserted pristine as-built 1960s values. 100 mm attic and EPS lambda=0.040 cases are sensitivity assumptions, not corrections to the active catalogue.",
    "Ground/slab and basement-wall calculations are one-dimensional assembly diagnostics. Soil, geometry, ground temperature, thermal bridges and ISO 13370 effective values are not reconstructed. Soil layers in the legacy basement slab are particularly provisional.",
    "Window layers, SHGC and VT remain pending. No glazing system is invented; only the existing LoD1 whole-window reference is shown.",
    "Do not fit insulation thickness to the LoD1 target. Active LoD1 anchors, curves, guardrails, explorer data and review notes remain unchanged."
  ],
